vscode: double-click, type
open: order.repository.ts

@brief
Eight times: `findMany` becomes `findOne`. End of the word, append,
`Ctrl-W`, type, out.

@keys
| `6e` | six word-ends forward |
| `a` | append |
| `Ctrl-W` | delete the word behind the cursor |

@hints
The stops are `return`, `this`, the dot, `orderRepository`, the dot,
`findMany`. Six.
--
The whole rep is one breath: land, append, wipe, type, escape. If you are
checking the screen after `Ctrl-W`, you are not there yet.

@solution
    6e  a  <Ctrl-W> findOne <Esc>  :wq<Enter>

Sixteen keystrokes and seven of them are the new name.

Worth noticing while you repeat it: you never once looked at where a
selection started or ended. The word boundary did that for you, the same
way on every rep, on a line you have not read carefully. That reliability
is what makes keyboard editing faster than pointing — not the keys
themselves.

@start order.repository.ts
    return this.orderRepository.findMany({ where: { id } });

@expected order.repository.ts
    return this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });
